# Copy this file to .claude/workflow.config in your project and edit it.
# Scripts under .claude/hooks and .claude/scripts read it via
# .claude/scripts/_config.sh — what you put here is just shell.

# =====================================================================
# Base-branch workflow (/base-pull, /base-push, /base-merge, /base-pr)
# =====================================================================

# The shared "trunk" branch other branches merge into and pull from.
# Common choices: main, master, trunk, develop.
WORKFLOW_BASE_BRANCH="main"

# Path to the canonical clone of the repo. Used by the transient-worktree
# helper to anchor the temporary worktrees it creates. Default is the
# current git toplevel — only set this if your "main clone" is somewhere
# different from the worktree you're calling skills from.
# WORKFLOW_MAIN_PATH="$HOME/code/myproject"

# =====================================================================
# Agent workflow (/agent-send, /agent-msg, /agent-rename) — all optional
# =====================================================================

# Pin an agent's identity in config. When set, fresh sessions in this
# project register under this name (overriding the current git branch),
# AND the recorded base branch is forced to this value — so the mismatch
# warning fires if the worktree is on a different branch.
#
# Precedence:
#   1. Session file's `name` field (from `/agent-rename` or `/rename`)
#   2. WORKFLOW_AGENT_DEFAULT_BRANCH (this knob)
#   3. Current git branch (sanitized)
#   4. cwd basename
#
# Example: "feature/foo" makes the agent name "feature-foo" (after the
# sanitization that turns / into -), regardless of which branch is
# checked out at startup.
# WORKFLOW_AGENT_DEFAULT_BRANCH=""

# Prepended to every auto-derived agent name. Useful when agents from
# multiple projects share one host and you want them prefixed by team
# or project. Example: "frontend-" → agent becomes "frontend-main".
# Applied AFTER the transform/sanitization steps below.
# WORKFLOW_AGENT_NAME_PREFIX=""

# Sed expression applied to the derived name BEFORE sanitization.
# Useful for stripping conventional branch prefixes.
# Example: "s|^feature/||" turns "feature/foo" into "foo".
# WORKFLOW_AGENT_NAME_TRANSFORM=""

# Set to "1" to skip the /rename keystroke that the SessionStart hook
# fires into the prompt buffer. The keystroke updates Claude's own
# session label (visible in the prompt box and the /resume picker) to
# match the registered agent name. Some users find that intrusive.
# WORKFLOW_AGENT_SKIP_RENAME=""

# Set to "1" to suppress the "you're on the wrong branch" warning
# the SessionStart hook emits when the worktree's branch doesn't
# match the recorded base. Useful in single-branch projects where
# the warning is noise.
# WORKFLOW_AGENT_SKIP_BRANCH_WARN=""

# Name of the agent that should run /base-test after a /todo continue.
# The todo skill's Mode 4 will dispatch the test notification to this
# agent unless the user overrides per-invocation.
# WORKFLOW_TESTING_AGENT=""

# =====================================================================
# Worktree workflow (/add-worktree, /remove-worktree, /list-worktrees)
# =====================================================================

# Parent directory for new worktrees. Default: parent directory of the
# current git toplevel. So if your repo is at ~/code/myproject, new
# worktrees land at ~/code/myproject-<name>. Set this to override.
# WORKFLOW_WORKTREE_PARENT="$HOME/code"

# Files to copy from the main clone to each new worktree at creation
# time. Useful for env files that are gitignored. Shell array.
# WORKFLOW_WORKTREE_COPY_FILES=(".env" ".env.local" ".envrc")

# Command to run inside each new worktree after creation (e.g. install
# deps). Default: no setup command. The /base-initialize skill does NOT
# run this by default — it's typically meaningful only after the user
# has configured their stack.
# WORKFLOW_WORKTREE_SETUP_CMD="pnpm install --frozen-lockfile"

# =====================================================================
# Ticketing integration (/define-tickets, generated /tickets skill)
# =====================================================================

# The ticketing-system project this repo's specs map to. Set by
# /define-tickets after the user picks a provider; consumed by the
# generated /tickets skill to scope every create/list/update call.
# Example values: "PROJ" (Jira), "ENG" (Linear), "owner/repo" (GitHub).
# WORKFLOW_PROJECT_ID=""

# The ticketing provider. Used by /define-tickets re-entry mode and by
# the generated /tickets skill for human-readable context.
# Common values: jira, linear, github, gitlab, asana, none.
# WORKFLOW_TICKET_PROVIDER=""

# How the generated /tickets skill talks to the provider:
#   mcp — call MCP server tools (e.g. atlassian/linear/github MCPs)
#   cli — wrap the provider's CLI (jira, linear, gh, glab)
#   api — direct HTTP calls with a token in .env
# WORKFLOW_TICKET_INTEGRATION=""
